Original code, 2026, Apache-2.0, except the explicitly attributed MIT adaptations
crypto/src/main/java/xyz/kd5ujc/scarab/crypto/vrf/Ed25519Point.java and Draft03Math.java. Their source
notices and fixtures/vrf/licenses/CCL-LICENSE are retained unchanged.

ledger/src/main/scala/xyz/kd5ujc/scarab/ledger/rules/MuslMath.scala and MuslData.scala are an MIT
adaptation too: a port of musl 1.2.5's double-precision log, pow and exp and their tables (src/math/log.c,
pow.c, exp.c and their _data.c files; Arm optimized-routines, Copyright (c) 2018, Arm Limited), so that the
pool-ranking likelihoods equal those of the statically linked reference node. musl's licence and copyright
notice are retained unchanged in ledger/licenses/LICENSE-musl. fixtures/reference/release-libm holds results
and table bytes measured from the reference node's release binary, which links that code.

crypto/src/main/java/com/weavechain (packages com.weavechain.curve25519 and com.weavechain.subtle) is
MIT code too: the source of curve25519-elisabeth, vendored from https://github.com/weavechain/curve25519-elisabeth at
81bd79dbd0b323e5fc5729bca883d124b95b4e54, the revision published as com.weavechain:curve25519-elisabeth:0.1.3
(a fork of cryptography-cafe/curve25519-elisabeth): MIT, Copyright (c) 2019 Jack Grigg. Portions derive from
eddsa-java (str4d/ed25519-java, CC0 1.0, itself a port of the public-domain ref10 Ed25519), and its
UnpackedScalar arithmetic (crypto/src/main/java/com/weavechain/curve25519/UnpackedScalar.java, whose SPDX
line adds BSD-3-Clause) was ported from curve25519-dalek (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2016-2018
Isis Agora Lovecruft, Henry de Valence). Its source notices are retained, and the upstream LICENSE with
all three notices is retained unchanged in crypto/licenses/LICENSE-curve25519-elisabeth; docs/licenses.md
records its provenance.

fixtures/reference/spending-datum contains generated throwaway private-network transactions
and original reference-node verdicts, produced by this project's Apache-2.0 tooling. Only public
verification keys and signatures are retained; no signing keys are distributed.
Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses.

fixtures/fuzz/early-era-transactions contains synthetic Shelley, Allegra and Mary decoder seeds
serialized by the Apache-2.0 reference CLI 11.2.3.0 bundled in node release 11.1.3. The input is
synthetic and witness sets are empty; no signing keys or ledger-admission claim are included.
The generated inputs are distributed under this project's Apache-2.0 license.

fixtures/reference/plutus-data-chunks contains synthetic CBOR inputs and original parser/hash
verdicts from the same reference CLI, under the project's Apache-2.0 license. No node was contacted.

fixtures/conway-flat-refusals contains digests of the bytes Scarab's own former flat Conway encoders
wrote for its test cases and the refusal corpus's Conway cases, and of the judgments of its former
flat Conway LEDGER, recorded by this project's Apache-2.0 tests before those were removed. They
are distributed under this project's Apache-2.0 license; no third-party material and no key is
included.

This source distribution includes test fixtures derived from Cardano Ledger,
Cardano Base, Ouroboros Network, Ouroboros Consensus, Amaru and Scalus-node.
Original upstream licenses and notices are retained under fixtures/licenses and
the per-fixture directories named below. No upstream implementation source is
vendored beyond the retained fixture/evidence excerpts and the curve25519-elisabeth
source named above.

Byron version fixtures (fixtures/byron-version): synthetic signed proposal generated by the
Apache-2.0 reference CLI 11.2.3.0 bundled in node release 11.1.3, plus byte-mutated
protocol-version fields and recorded raw decoder verdicts. Only the throwaway key's public
verification key and signature are retained; no signing key is included. Upstream notices
for the reference ledger are retained in fixtures/licenses.

Network fixtures (fixtures/network): manually specified and source-derived
handshake, mux, BlockFetch and KeepAlive envelopes from Ouroboros Network
(KeepAlive pin: commit c45735a56c567fa977969173d18943bac6bb3821) and Scalus-node,
plus Ouroboros Consensus-derived payloads, all Apache-2.0. Licenses and NOTICE
files are retained in fixtures/licenses, and the KeepAlive license beside
fixtures/network/keepalive-direct-range/manifest.json. Source-derived envelopes
are not captured upstream runtime transcripts. The Scala implementation is
independent.

VRF (fixtures/vrf): the draft03 verifier adapts Bloxbean CCL Ed25519Point.java
and VrfUtil.java at commit 45906b783973b4c44ac6883253af26bdd07bc1b4 under MIT.
The full CCL copyright/permission notice is retained in
fixtures/vrf/licenses/CCL-LICENSE. Cardano sodium source-derived public
fixtures retain the ISC notice in fixtures/vrf/licenses/sodium-LICENSE.
Bouncy Castle's notice is retained alongside it. No native binary, prover,
signer or keygen is bundled.

Ed25519 witnesses (fixtures/witness): public-only sodium, speccheck, Wycheproof
and ledger fixture projections with their ISC, Apache-2.0 and MIT/CC0/BSD
attribution files in fixtures/witness/licenses. The curve25519-elisabeth arithmetic
is vendored source (named above); the fixtures hold no signing implementation or
private-key corpus.

Wycheproof Ed25519 (fixtures/wycheproof-ed25519): the C2SP/wycheproof Ed25519
verification vectors at commit a3d5d1423f2592d6646836a45a21a1b209da9f4d, Apache-2.0,
with Wycheproof's LICENSE beside them. The reference verdicts and the driver that
produced them are Scarab's own; the libsodium source the driver builds is not
redistributed.

ECVRF draft-03 vectors (fixtures/vrf-cardano-base): the seven vrf_ver03 test vectors of
IntersectMBO/cardano-base revision 060819b59c184b951a54e3c563304983c53a3eac, Apache-2.0
(fixtures/licenses/cardano-base-LICENSE and cardano-base-NOTICE). Their seeds are
published test keys.

VRF proof-to-hash cases (fixtures/vrf-proof-to-hash): proofs derived from those
cardano-base vectors (Apache-2.0, the same licence files), with the results of the
pinned libsodium fork's crypto_vrf_ietfdraft03_proof_to_hash. The results and the driver
that produced them are Scarab's own; the libsodium source is not redistributed.

Leios (fixtures/leios): serialisation test vectors from IntersectMBO/cardano-base
(Apache-2.0; fixtures/licenses/cardano-base-LICENSE and -NOTICE), the golden LeiosVote of
IntersectMBO/ouroboros-consensus branch leios-prototype (Apache-2.0), and the throwaway
proto-devnet BLS test keys and genesis proofs of input-output-hk/ouroboros-leios (Apache-2.0).
Provenance per file is in fixtures/leios/README.md. The recorded testnet handshake replies are
protocol bytes. The ledger snapshots in fixtures/leios/state were written by the Leios testnet image
(input-output-hk/ouroboros-leios, Apache-2.0, not redistributed): two on a throwaway local devnet,
and testnet-2168639/state by a node following the public Leios testnet, public chain data of a
test network holding public keys and hashes only. Provenance is in fixtures/leios/state/README.md.

Operational certificates (fixtures/opcert): the exact ledger OCert source and
four public Amaru header fixtures with their Apache-2.0 LICENSE/NOTICE files
under fixtures/opcert/evidence. The Scala adapter is original public-only code.

Sum6 KES (fixtures/sum6) and Praos headers (fixtures/praos): source-derived from
IntersectMBO/cardano-base revision 060819b59c184b951a54e3c563304983c53a3eac,
Apache-2.0, with public Amaru header fixtures under the Amaru license. Retained
sources and exact-target LICENSE files are under the respective evidence
directories; original notices remain in those files. Immutable pins are in
fixtures/sum6/evidence/sources.json.

The Conway ledger-derived witness fixtures originate in the Haskell
cardano-ledger-conformance-tests, distributed through cardano-blueprint and
Amaru; their verbatim licenses are fixtures/licenses/cardano-ledger-conformance-LICENSE,
cardano-ledger-conformance-NOTICE, blueprint-conformance-LICENSE and amaru-LICENSE.

Captured chain data (fixtures/mainnet, fixtures/preview, fixtures/mempack): public blockchain data fetched from the
public Cardano relays (fixtures/mempack: 95 ledger outputs of the Mithril preprod snapshot); fixtures/preview also holds records derived from the Koios public API
(https://koios.rest). fixtures/reference/leios-testnet-chain-contexts and fixtures/reference/leios-testnet-chain-scripts
hold transactions, spent outputs and script arguments of the public Leios testnet's chain (network magic 164), read
from a node of the testnet's own build that followed it. fixtures/eras, fixtures/haskell-state (ledger snapshots written by the reference
node 11.1.3 tooling) and fixtures/kes-gen are produced from a throwaway local cluster
and carry no third-party data. fixtures/dijkstra-devnet is produced from a throwaway local cluster of the
Leios testnet image of input-output-hk/ouroboros-leios (Apache-2.0); its Alonzo, Conway and Dijkstra
genesis files are derived from that testnet's (provenance in fixtures/dijkstra-devnet/README.md).
fixtures/reference/dijkstra-state-translation holds what the unchanged cardano-ledger (Apache-2.0) of the
Leios testnet build computes from the throwaway local-cluster snapshot in fixtures/leios/state (provenance
in fixtures/reference/dijkstra-state-translation/README.md), and fixtures/reference/leios-ntc-queries what it answers
to two node-to-client queries on the state files there (provenance in fixtures/reference/leios-ntc-queries/README.md).
fixtures/reference/dijkstra-epoch holds the ledger states the same cardano-ledger reaches when it ticks two of those state files across
Dijkstra's epoch boundaries (provenance in fixtures/reference/dijkstra-epoch/README.md).
fixtures/reference/leios-testnet-context-refusals holds, under the project's licence (Apache-2.0), synthetic Dijkstra
transactions Scarab generates and the results recorded for them. The transactions carry placeholder scripts and no
chain data, and are set in the public Leios testnet's environment (its public protocol version, cost models, system
start and slot length, as fixtures/reference/leios-testnet-chain-contexts records them); the results are the verdicts
the unchanged cardano-ledger (Apache-2.0) of the pinned Leios testnet build gives on them, run in an image built from
it that is not redistributed (provenance in fixtures/reference/leios-testnet-context-refusals/README.md).
fixtures/reference/refusals holds, under the project's licence (Apache-2.0), transactions Scarab's tooling built and
signed with throwaway keys of private local devnets, the genesis files of those devnets, and the refusals and ledger
states the unchanged official cardano-node release (Apache-2.0) recorded for them; only public verification keys,
key hashes and signatures are retained, and no signing key is distributed (provenance in
fixtures/reference/refusals/README.md and each corpus's corpus.json). fixtures/reference/genesis-fields holds, under
the same licence, changes Scarab generates to the repository's genesis files and the verdicts the unchanged released
cardano-ledger (Apache-2.0) parsers give on them, run in an image built from it that is not redistributed
(provenance in fixtures/reference/genesis-fields/README.md and provenance.json).
fixtures/reference/dijkstra-pparams holds, under the project's licence (Apache-2.0), synthetic Dijkstra
protocol-parameter updates Scarab generates and what the unchanged cardano-ledger (Apache-2.0) of the pinned Leios
testnet build makes of them, run in an image built from it that is not redistributed (provenance in
fixtures/reference/dijkstra-pparams/README.md).
The files in fixtures/licenses and the licence files of the
individual fixture directories cover the upstream-derived test vectors.

